cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or reference this specification, please cite it as below."
title: "Wildlife Detection Exchange (WDX): an open interchange format for AI wildlife detections from community-run sensors"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Rajiah"
    given-names: "Arun"
    city: "Chennai"
    country: "IN"
version: "0.1"
date-released: "2026-08-25"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/arunrajiah/wildlife-detection-exchange"
keywords:
  - bioacoustics
  - camera traps
  - biodiversity informatics
  - Darwin Core
  - machine observation
  - BirdNET
  - Perch
  - SpeciesNet
  - data standard
abstract: >
  WDX is a lightweight JSON interchange format for machine-generated wildlife
  detection events from continuous community-run sensors such as BirdNET
  acoustic stations and AI-classified camera traps. Each event carries taxon,
  location, time, classifier identity and version, confidence, media reference
  and human review status, and maps field by field to Darwin Core so that any
  WDX stream can be exported as a standard occurrence dataset with
  basisOfRecord MachineObservation and published to GBIF. Version 0.1 is a
  draft proposal published to anchor community discussion and reference
  implementations.
